{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts","id":347850,"title":"Ventrue / Julii Historical Impacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-22T16:47:02-08:00","id":347850,"title":"Ventrue / Julii Historical Impacts","content":"Do any of the books have information on Ventrue or Julii that existed prior to Rome?<br /> <br /> Did either of these Clans have any impact on world affairs before Rome, or were they 'born' in the Roman nights? For example, would ancient Egypt or mezzo-America have Ventrue and/or Julii around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:19:18-08:00","id":347871,"title":"","content":"<i>Shadows of Mexico</i> mentions an extinct group of vampires that resembled the European Ventrue before the Europeans arrived. I don't think remember <i>Requiem for Rome </i>placing the Ventrue anywhere. It makes it sound as if North Africa just had Gangrel, Mekhet and Nosferatu before the other clans came. The Bron have at least one origin story that has no connection to anyone outside the British Isles or any existing vampires for that matter. That's in one of the bloodline books I think. I'm guessing that sometimes Gangrel populations produce Ventrue splinters that don't appear in history until they're well established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:45:40-08:00","id":347880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm guessing that sometimes Gangrel populations produce Ventrue splinters that don't appear in history until they're well established. </div> </div> </div>This is what I generally support as Ventrue origins, they are in fact Gangrel bloodline that adapted better to urban society then the main Clan and the only bloodline so far to achieve Clan status. Julii were IMO a seperate Clan who pacted with some power (maybe Strix, maybe not) for their immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:46:54-08:00","id":347882,"title":"","content":"The Devs have been explicit about the Julii, they were born in Rome and they died there. So the intent is that the Julii cannot be found elsewhere/did not survive as a clan.<br /> <br /> Ventrue could've emerged pretty much anywhere. Think convergent evolution rather than an obvious line of descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T18:24:50-08:00","id":347923,"title":"","content":"According to Ancient Mysteries, the Ventrue go as far back as most other Clans. There were even Ventrue in Ancient Egypt or at least vampires we would identify as Ventrue today. The question is what does this say about Ventrue-Gangrel connection?<br /> <br /> Perhaps they are related, but actually split of multiple times? Once in the mists of history in Mesopotamia and Egypt and later on in Europe towards the end of the Roman Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 12-22-2014, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:38:24-08:00","id":347970,"title":"","content":"Lords Over the Damned suggests that the Ventrue and Julii were once one clan, until one of them illegally embraced the grandson of the king Ascanius and his childer were subsequently exiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones.