T17:32:35-08:00","id":348658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=348652#post348652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed that the Julli were a family or Bloodline of Ventrue who made a deal with the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition in one section came out and said that Nosferatu were a relatively new clan . But however there was an old clan of something very nos like in ancient times.<br /> Perhaps a similar situation exists between the ventrue and Jullii?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T12:42:17-08:00","id":349228,"title":"","content":"What about the Traditores? Are they referenced anywhere else?<br /> <br /> It just seems so weird that Rome spawned two unique Clans that never get mentioned again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T14:38:41-08:00","id":349293,"title":"","content":"On a more practical note, has anyone played a Requiem for Rome game that lasted beyond the fall of the Camarilla and the Roman Empire? Did you have Julii player characters in the group? Did they survive into future eras, and if so how did you handle their continued existence in a world where their clan is meant to be gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T15:08:01-08:00","id":349329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=349293#post349293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more practical note, has anyone played a Requiem for Rome game that lasted beyond the fall of the Camarilla and the Roman Empire? Did you have Julii player characters in the group? Did they survive into future eras, and if so how did you handle their continued existence in a world where their clan is meant to be gone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I played in a chronicle that was a series of one-shot games, each a flashpoint in history, with us all playing the same characters or sometimes our previous characters' childer or grandchilder. We started in Rome, and those of us who wanted to play Ventrue in later flashpoints just played different characters for the first session who all died in the fall. One guy who played a Julii for that game actually had it worked out with the ST that his character was possessed by a Strix the whole time and none of the rest of us knew until after he turned on us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T05:56:17-07:00","id":1345208,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know it's damned topic necromancy, but it fits my question perfectly. So let's do foul rites on All Hallows now... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>WHEN Julii where no more and Ventrue took their place, especially in Byzantium? </b>Julii are clearly pure Roman Clan, described to fell with West Empire itself. Ventru name is french for 'potbellied' - and even Clan itself says tells they have common origin with Julii from Troy, only their sprinter founder went to Gaul.<br /> <br /> With vampires easily living century, two more than mortals - that meant that last Julii in Rome would die, when, circa 670 AD ( as Rome fell to Goths in 476 AD )? With coming of Charles Martel frankish Empire in 718 AD - and letter, Charlemagne becoming 'Emperor of Romans' in 800 AD - it sounds as good time for spread of Ventrue on the Western Europe, with Frankish rules on those terrains, spreading Frankish Ventrue Clan all around it.<br /> <br /> But what with Eastern Roman Empire, i.e. Byzantium? Emperors of it from circa 500 are random mix of Greeks, previous Romans, Balkans and Slavic nobles, all mixed with one another, as crown is 'jumping' around many pretenders, not setting proper dynasty. It does not sound as good environment for supporting Julii lineages in area - and Ventrue seems to be too far, not until like 900 AD, when Byzantium makes constant contacts with Empire of Franks. What do you think about topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T06:49:07-07:00","id":1345217,"title":"","content":"<b>Ancient Mysteries</b> quote, from page 155, seems to solve my question on Byzantium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient Mysteries, p. 155</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Athanatoi, who considered themselves the direct descendants of a more-or-less unbroken Camarilla (the Patriarch and Imperator during the Crusade Era were both said to have been Embraced prior to the fall of Rome).</div> </div> </div> </div>So if Imperator is Embraced before fall of Rome, it means it's late 5th century, so he should be from Julii Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:23:48-07:00","id":1345258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345217#post1345217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ancient Mysteries</b> quote, from page 155, seems to solve my question on Byzantium.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So if Imperator is Embraced before fall of Rome, it means it's late 5th century, so he should be from Julii Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not true. You misunderstand the Julii in this regard. They were the Clan of Rome. Not Romans. Rome. The &quot;Queen of Cities&quot;. Even as the Roman Empire decayed and the capital of that Empire migrated to more defensible locations (Ravenna, etc.) the Julii remained buried in Rome like ticks, pulling the strings of their Camarilla and acting like it was the heyday of the Republic.<br /> <br /> They didn't like to leave, and certainly didn't like to travel. Doing so put them at risk of being influenced by ethereal critters. Doing so took them away from what mattered: Rome and its power manipulations. They could easily leverage their position and contacts to send &quot;lesser clans&quot; out to accomplish the administration of the Camarilla's vassal princedoms, and did so. Thus, assuming that a minor regional city such as Byzantium might get a Julii honcho just because the latest upstart human emperor renamed it Constantinople is to ascribe human motivations and sensibilities to human power on top of these ancient monsters. <br /> <br /> Yes, you did have some Julii who went into exile away from Rome--perhaps for a time or voluntarily, but they tended to come back or be on assignment until an objective was reached. The Legio Mortuus--paradoxically one of the safest ways for Julii to travel, was the adopted home of more martial clans, as well.<br /> <br /> So no, the Imperator doesn't need to be Julii. And further, the assault on the Julii themselves was not limited to the City of Rome: they were ALL targeted by the Strix. It was a great conspiracy and the Ventrue <b><i>might</i></b> have been intimately behind it. They were certainly the powers behind the barbarian tribes at the time. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:31:38-07:00","id":1345261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345258#post1345258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not true. You misunderstand the Julii in this regard. They were the Clan of Rome. Not Romans. Rome. The &quot;Queen of Cities&quot;. Even as the Roman Empire decayed and the capital of that Empire migrated to more defensible locations (Ravenna, etc.) the Julii remained buried in Rome like ticks, pulling the strings of their Camarilla and acting like it was the heyday of the Republic.<br /> <br /> They didn't like to leave, and certainly didn't like to travel. Doing so put them at risk of being influenced by ethereal critters. Doing so took them away from what mattered: Rome and its power manipulations. They could easily leverage their position and contacts to send &quot;lesser clans&quot; out to accomplish the administration of the Camarilla's vassal princedoms, and did so. Thus, assuming that a minor regional city such as Byzantium might get a Julii honcho just because the latest upstart human emperor renamed it Constantinople is to ascribe human motivations and sensibilities to human power on top of these ancient monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so Julii would not move to the Byzantium just because it seems to them as 'too fresh', before fall of Rome. With Daevas being 'filling ranks' of Lancea Sanctum - with their all need for appeasement of crowd - two major political Clans are out of Emperors seats race. Gangrel seems too wild to sit on Night Emperors throne in years circa 700. Mekhet and Nosferatu just seems not interested in those kinds political games. And Ventrue are at least two centuries before real constant contact to fill the ranks of Emperors in Byzantium... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This why I think that making Night Emperor as one last Julii ruling Byzantine Kindred could be good idea - he is last of his kind, staying alive from the Roman line. Strix are hunting on him, and rest just want's to pull his threads. One bad move, and first coming Ventrues will take his crown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2019, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:42:06-07:00","id":1345267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345258#post1345258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, the Imperator doesn't need to be Julii. And further, the assault on the Julii themselves was not limited to the City of Rome: they were ALL targeted by the Strix. It was a great conspiracy and the Ventrue <b><i>might</i></b> have been intimately behind it. They were certainly the powers behind the barbarian tribes at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>This 'powers behind barbarian tribes' part can be really game changer.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I thought that all barbarians - Slavs, Vandals, Bulgars and rest of 'wartime neighbors' of Byzantium - were breading lands for Gangrel, all along. IF they were also infiltrated by Ventrues, from 500+ AD, not on 900+ AD, it's much more logical that Emperor could be one new 'foreign' noble from barbarians that become native - like many famous Byzantine generals, later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T10:44:29-07:00","id":1345269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345261#post1345261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so Julii would not move to the Byzantium just because it seems to them as 'too fresh', before fall of Rome. With Daevas being 'filling ranks' of Lancea Sanctum - with their all need for appeasement of crowd - two major political Clans are out of Emperors seats race. Gangrel seems too wild to sit on Night Emperors throne in years circa 700. Mekhet and Nosferatu just seems not interested in those kinds political games. And Ventrue are at least two centuries before real constant contact to fill the ranks of Emperors in Byzantium... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This why I think that making Night Emperor as one last Julii ruling Byzantine Kindred is good idea - he is last of his kind, staying alive from the Roman line. Strix are hunting on him, and rest just want's to pull his threads. One bad move, and first coming Ventrues will take his crown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your call mate--certainly SOME Julii did survive the purge. There are books listing them as characters. The sudden disappearance of the Julii is both convenient to the Ventrue and something I'd expect them to play up on over time, while in actuality the ascension of the Ventrue to power was more gradual than they'd like to suggest.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking we can assume the Ventrue were more associated with migrating tribes prior to the rise of feudal states such as the Franks. Constantinople was affected by but never fell to such tribes. Most likely the Prince (or even King of the ERE) was Daeva (hedonistic power) or Mekhet (famous schemers). I'd side with Mekhet, though WoD created a triumvirate between a [Daeva], Nos and Tzimisce. You could do something similar (Daeva, Mekhet, Nos) and rotate the roles of Prince of the city, King/Emperor of the East, and torpic elder voice between them. Give them each a set of favored &quot;speaker&quot; lackeys who carry the elder's favor and (when they are in torpor) speak with the elder's voice.<br /> <br /> I'll probably use some structure like this. It would be pretty stable so long as you treat it as a PC coterie that turned NPC--in other words they actually liked each other, once.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS Edit: A few additional points on the Ventrue. They were lords of the migrating barbarians. They may have been lords in Troy, come to Rome (and Carthage), and been expelled as the Julii became what they are. The Ventrue <b><i>may</i></b> be an offshoot of the Julii, or the Julii an offshoot of the Ventrue (this is more likely in my opinion). <br /> <br /> In any case, the Ventrue were banned from Rome itself but existed as &quot;lords&quot; among the barbarians in their core peoples, washing back and forth around the Empire as it became progressively less stable. The question you may want to answer, as it will explain origins more, is whether or not these Lords knew to stay out of Rome thanks to oral tradition, or simply did so because the Julii made it quite impervious to their presence?<br /> <br /> If the former, then you have a thousand-year conspiracy between the/a Ventrue progenitor and his or her extended line with the Strix, culminating in the Julii's well-deserved murder. In the latter you have the Ventrue and their Gangrel allies gathering a fatal strike at the heart of the tottering Camarilla, and the Strix riding (literally) along for their own pleasure and revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  More speculation on Ventrue 11-01-2019, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T11:06:30-07:00","id":1345275,"title":"","content":"<b>I like to run vampires, on general, as 'insects enclosed in amber' comparing to mortal society.</b> They do not like changes, on general, and do not like to change roles in society. That's why I would simply stay out of Triumvirate option, rotating on Torpor. It's messy and destebelize vampric society too much - so they not like it. Now to Ventrue...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345269#post1345269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS Edit: A few additional points on the Ventrue. They were lords of the migrating barbarians. They may have been lords in Troy, come to Rome (and Carthage), and been expelled as the Julii became what they are. The Ventrue <b><i>may</i></b> be an offshoot of the Julii, or the Julii an offshoot of the Ventrue (this is more likely in my opinion).<br /> <br /> In any case, the Ventrue were banned from Rome itself but existed as &quot;lords&quot; among the barbarians in their core peoples, washing back and forth around the Empire as it became progressively less stable. The question you may want to answer, as it will explain origins more, is whether or not these Lords knew to stay out of Rome thanks to oral tradition, or simply did so because the Julii made it quite impervious to their presence?<br /> <br /> If the former, then you have a thousand-year conspiracy between the/a Ventrue progenitor and his or her extended line with the Strix, culminating in the Julii's well-deserved murder. In the latter you have the Ventrue and their Gangrel allies gathering a fatal strike at the heart of the tottering Camarilla, and the Strix riding (literally) along for their own pleasure and revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>In both yours scenarios we have Gangrel AND Ventrue in barbarians tribes</b>, where I with my passing knowledge of <b>VtR</b> thought that only vampires in 'uncivilized wilds' were Gangrel. If Ventrues are 'normal' sight to be seen in barbaric armies of first millenium till 500 AD, scenario with 'wild Ven becoming Constantinopole Emperor' is much more possible and elegant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like, I just read on about 4-5 wars with barbarians that Byzantium made on their soil in year 500 till 600 only, with Byzantine generals being ex-barbarians themselves. With living giving Emperor title to previous barbarians constantly from 400+ AD, Kindred can make exactly the same. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2019, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T11:46:04-07:00","id":1345289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/347850-ventrue-julii-historical-impacts?p=1345261#post1345261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet and Nosferatu just seems not interested in those kinds political games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the very same book the Mekhet are leading the Great Covenant, the first known unified Kindred society that basically was the Camarilla before the Camarilla. Admittedly they do so in a primarily religious capacity, but I also want to point out that Clan stereotypes are merely stereotypes, and that all Clans are composed out of individuals who can follow or break the stereotypes as much as they please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:59:45-07:00","id":1345313,"title":"","content":"My take ( at least for now ) on Night Imperator origin in Constantinopole, connected to Ventrue-Julii debate....<br /> <br /> Nowadays rules of Imperator and Prisci Council ( 700-1000 AD ) is result of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Justinian Plague</a> of 541 ( with it\u2019s repeated resurgences till 750 AD ) \u2013 called centuries later Black Death. With as high as 40% mortality rate in Empire, it took many of humans supplies and networks of older Roman Elders \u2013 leading to their downfall or even Final Death. With humans dying en masse and normal dead returning to 'life' \u2013 Kindred needed change of rules. With old Patriarch lost in tumult and Prisci Council finally dead, vampires looked for new leaders. It came with <i>Ventranis</i> \u2013 previous barbarians hordes leader from West that became general in Days Emperor armies. He with few others Ancillae helped new appointed Patriarch Ivonius enforced order in Plague stricken Constantinopole. Following traditions of living Eastern Roman Empire, he was anointed <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ( Great Night Imperator ) by Ivonius \u2013 and start it\u2019s rules as King ( or rather, Emperor ) of Reigning City. He appointed his helpers as Prisci that now advise him in ranks of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine%E2%80%99s-empire-kindred\">Athnatoi</a>. Researchers in Imperial Library whispers that they found legend about Imperator\u2019s name giver \u2013 <i>Ven</i> \u2013 being connected to stories of Troy and creation of Julii Clan of old\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T22:59:43-08:00","id":1345711,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that as of <b>A Thousand Years of Night</b>, the Julii and Ventrue have different clan banes AND different clan disciplines. 2nd edition has chosen to emphasize the differences between them. That said, if at your table, the Julii turned into the Ventrue, that is okay.<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine they two clans were very competitive with one another. It would come as no surprise to me that the Camarilla banned the Ventrue from Roman territory as they did the Traditores, but i don't think that was ever confirmed. In fact I used to think the Ventrue were the Traditores until one of the writers/devs said they were meant to be the Akhud.<br /> Which is what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3386_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3386\" data-vbnamecard=\"3386\">Piff</a> asked about, so I feel comfortable sharing that here.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Byzantine Julii, the last one is said to have vanished in 418 CE, with a scream. At least according to <b>Fall of the Camarilla</b>, page 196. So yes they existed, but they certainly aren't in the public eye when the Great Night Imperator showed up centuries later. That said, you can change that at your table and there is nothing to say the Byzantine Julii did not go into hiding. There were rumours of Sanctified assassins offing them around that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T02:41:59-08:00","id":1345739,"title":"","content":"It's pretty likely that at least some Julii did indeed turn into Ventrue (considering how Licinii were mentioned as a Ventrue bloodline before being written as a Julii bloodline, and the Ventrue bloodline Macellarius taking name, appearance, behaviour, history and basically everything from the Julius Macellarius Corbulo). Whether or not that's the origin of the Ventrue Clan is less sure. On one hand the Ventrue simply did not exist in Central America until after Europeans found the place according to Shadows of Mexico, but on the other hand Ancient Mysteries mentions Ventrue as part of the Great Covenant. The book does use the name Ventrue for both Ventrue and Julii, but that's in Egypt about 500 years before the Roman <i>Monarchy</i> was formed. It can only have been Julii if they significantly predated Romulus and Remus as well as having a notable presence outside of Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:17:43-08:00","id":1345781,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=wyrdhamster;n1345275]<b>I like to run vampires, on general, as 'insects enclosed in amber' comparing to mortal society.</b> They do not like changes, on general, and do not like to change roles in society. That's why I would simply stay out of Triumvirate option, rotating on Torpor. It's messy and destebelize vampric society too much - so they not like it. Now to Ventrue...<br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Your (Ventrue) plotline is at least plausible. Personally I like throwing in Justinian and Theodora as vamps--perhaps acting as figureheads or something? They got some <b><i>fascinating </i></b>supernatural bad press later in life!<br /> <br /> However regarding the above, may I gently point out that as much as the vampires would like to avoid &quot;rotating on Torpor&quot; it's going to happen regardless. The only question is whether a system is put in place to manage this. <br /> <br /> Just to avoid some dissonance for you, also note please that VtR 2e vamps are very much not &quot;insects encased in amber&quot;--that would be true of WoD vamps and to a lesser extent VtR 1e, however the tone broke severely toward dynamic vamps that reinvent themselves constantly using, not incidentally, torpor. Vamps that don't do this become ossified and, well, ashes.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:34:43-08:00","id":1345787,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. This really clarifies a lot. I read Thousand Years of Night, but I never read any of the earlier stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:18:48-08:00","id":1345843,"title":"","content":"Dominate is an interesting Discipline. I've always felt like there's a bit of a hex on it, like it attaches itself to clans and then rings them out for all they're worth. Maybe that's confusing correlation and causation, but other &quot;Dominate clans&quot; have staked a claim in the All Night Society, and all seem to have suffered nasty ends. We know about the Dead Julii, obviously, and the Kindred of Central America remember a bloodline of tyrants who met their destruction at the hands of their slaves. European vampires tend to assume these tyrants were Lords doing Lord things, but they also assume that about the Julii.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue, of course, were active in other parts of the New World. Just ask the Tsihstekeri in Montreal. They say they're Ventrue. They say the Lords ruled the nights of Turtle Island long before the colonial period.<br /> <br /> They're right, of course. They are Ventrue.<br /> <br /> What they <i>were</i>, though? Never mind that. Vampires never tell the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-05-2019, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}